// Host-conformance fixture: verifier closes its stdin WITHOUT reading the
// request, then writes a schema-valid `deny code=malformed_input` at exit 0.
// This is the §6 bound-exceeded shape (stop reading, emit malformed_input).
// Because §2 obligates the host to write the whole request and then EOF, the
// read end closing under the host's write surfaces as EPIPE/SIGPIPE on the
// host side — a request-delivery failure §7.2 does not enumerate. The host
// MUST still produce a deny (relay this deny, or fail closed on its own write
// failure) and MUST NOT crash or hang. Offered case: verdict is well-formed;
// the only misbehavior is that the request was never consumed.
require('fs').closeSync(0);
